[issue.1748]
number = 1748
title = "[Coherence] The finality proof scenario never makes reward authorization depend on the authenticated SnapshotBinding"
revision = "a910fdedd579e63379ae6c2e4d4971990d28f8ad"
verdict = "task"
evidence = "The proof added by commit a98636f083ddfcbfc01d2e65b588721e4c20f38d still checks witnesses in test-local CommittedRead::verify at programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market/tests/repair_22_33_261.rs:1043 using the fixed key at :1140, then sends CLAIM with only worker, recipient and amount at :1158 and the binding's height at :1233; SnapshotBinding remains confined to queries.rs in the guest source at programs/crates/layerx-programs-ai-market/src/queries.rs:693, while the production consumer already exists in services/agent/crates/layerx-client/src/ai_market.rs:604 and :850, so spec/layerx-merge/spec.kvx:197854 still needs a regression that connects witness refusal to that consumer's reward authorization."
close_comment = "The finality scenario rejects tampered witnesses separately from the reward action, so it does not prove that reward authorization requires an authenticated snapshot. A focused regression task will exercise the existing client consumer from committed state verification through CLAIM preparation and approval, including refusal of modified or missing evidence."

